      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Imperforate hymen is a rare occurrence in younger women resulting in hydrocolpos and hydrometrocolpos. Though imperforate hymen may be diagnosed in infancy, females ages 9-15 years most often present with the problem. Imperforate hymen usually is a congenital anomaly, but has been reported as a result of sexual abuse. This case report reviews the presentation and treatment of a 13-year-old female with imperforate hymen."},
